---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { identityLong } from "../../data/program";

// The research page — the fuller version of the homepage's research + projects,
// kept consistent with it. The four current projects (B1–B4) are defined here for
// this page.
const projects = [
  {
    title: "Three Ways of Leaving p Unsettled",
    tag: "Formal semantics · in progress",
    href: null,
    current: true,
    desc: "A formal-semantics and pragmatics paper on three things everyday talk files under “uncertainty”: saying something might be so, saying it might or might not be, and saying you don’t know whether it is. Each leaves a different question open and licenses a different reply — the paper pins the distinction down. Currently under review by a formal semanticist.",
  },
  {
    title: "Master’s thesis — is meaning like this learnable?",
    tag: "Thesis · in design",
    href: null,
    desc: "Takes that distinction and asks a learnability question: trained on realistic input, does a small language model come to hold a possibility open and reason about it — and what in the input does that take? Formal analysis sets the target; a controlled corpus-and-training experiment tests it.",
  },
  {
    title: "Cross-lingual ProtoBias",
    tag: "First-author paper",
    href: "/research/cross-lingual-protobias",
    desc: "A first-author paper: a controlled cross-lingual audit — hold the image pair fixed, vary only the prompt language, and test whether vision-language judges track meaning or a culture-specific prototype. ~12,600 judgments across seven languages and two model families; public code, arXiv in preparation.",
  },
  {
    title: "Latent Control States",
    tag: "Collaboration · DFKI",
    href: null,
    desc: "With DFKI: does prompt framing shift a causally relevant latent state, or only the output? My part is a utilitarian minimal-pair probe — dilemma × benefit-size × framing — testing whether the model’s choice tracks the real stakes or just surface pressure.",
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Research · Xiaochuan Li"
  description="Experimental and computational semantics: how linguistic expressions structure information — which possibilities stay open, which are ruled out, what can be taken up in later reasoning — and how that structure is acquired by people and learned by language models."
>
  <article class="rx">
    <h1 class="rx-h1">Research</h1>
    <p class="rx-lede">{identityLong}</p>
    <p class="rx-lede">
      The throughline is one question: how linguistic expressions structure information — which
      possibilities remain open, which are ruled out, and what can be taken up in later reasoning —
      and how much of that structure is acquired by people and learned by models.
    </p>

    <section class="rx-sec">
      <h2 class="rx-h2">The current question</h2>
      <p class="rx-p">
        Everyday talk files a lot of things under “uncertainty”, but they are not the same. Saying
        <em>the key might be in the drawer</em> leaves that possibility open. Saying <em>it might be,
        or it might not</em> explicitly opens both sides. Saying <em>I don’t know whether it is</em>
        reports that you cannot settle the question at all. Each leaves a different question open in
        the discourse, and each licenses a different reply and a different next move.
      </p>
      <p class="rx-p">
        My current paper — formal semantics and pragmatics — pins that three-way distinction down.
        The thesis then asks the learnability question: whether a language model, trained on
        realistic input, comes to treat these the way a competent speaker does, and what in the input
        that would take. The point of the model is not that it resembles a mind; it is a system whose
        entire input is linguistic, so it bounds what linguistic distribution alone can deliver.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="rx-sec">
      <h2 class="rx-h2">Projects</h2>
      <div class="rx-projs">
        {projects.map((p) => (
          <div class={`rx-proj${p.current ? " rx-proj-current" : ""}`}>
            <div class="rx-proj-top">
              {p.href
                ? <a class="rx-proj-title" href={p.href}>{p.title}</a>
                : <span class="rx-proj-title-plain">{p.title}</span>}
              <span class="rx-proj-tag">{p.tag}</span>
            </div>
            <p class="rx-proj-desc">{p.desc}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <p class="rx-foot">
      More on where this came from is in the <a href="/writing">writing</a>; the front page has the
      short version and a timeline.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .rx { max-width: 42rem; }
  .rx-h1 { font-size: 1.6rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.01em; margin: 0 0 1rem; color: var(--color-text); }
  .rx-lede { font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--color-text-muted); margin: 0 0 1rem; max-width: 40rem; }
  .rx-lede:first-of-type { color: var(--color-text); }

  .rx-sec { margin-top: 2.8rem; }
  .rx-h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-text-dim);
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.6rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }
  .rx-p { font-size: 0.96rem; line-height: 1.72; color: var(--color-text-muted); margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .rx-p em { font-style: italic; color: var(--color-text); }

  .rx-projs { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .rx-proj { padding: 1.1rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .rx-proj:first-child { border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .rx-proj-top {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }
  .rx-proj-title { font-size: 1.04rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--color-text); text-decoration: none; }
  .rx-proj-title:hover { color: var(--color-accent); }
  .rx-proj-title-plain { font-size: 1.04rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--color-text); }
  .rx-proj-tag {
    flex: none;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-text-dim);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .rx-proj-current .rx-proj-tag { color: var(--color-accent); }
  .rx-proj-desc { font-size: 0.93rem; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--color-text-muted); margin: 0; max-width: 60ch; }

  .rx-foot { margin-top: 2.4rem; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--color-text-dim); }
  .rx-foot a { color: var(--color-accent); text-decoration: none; }
  .rx-foot a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
</style>
